W109 measurement instrumentation: see WHY the window is black.

Purely additive logging. No behaviour changes, no register decode changes, no
framebuffer address changes, nothing painted. Every number in docs/W109-RESULTS.md
comes from these lines.

The headline finding, which refuted the brief's lead: the 114688-byte packet is a
VU1 XGKICK, not a display register walk. It reaches the GS via
PS2Memory::submitGifPacket(Path1,...) in ps2_vu1_core.cpp, which BYPASSES both
PS2Memory::processGIFPacket overloads -- so the first two dumps here printed nothing,
which is itself the proof it is not the EE DMA path.

The decisive result: [frame:census] and [frame:channels] show the framebuffer is
NOT empty. 286720 of 286720 pixels are present, every one of them (0,0,0,255):
full alpha, zero colour. Coverage works; the colour path does not.

